WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.635
These new weight-loss medications

00:00:01.635 --> 00:00:06.039
are hailed
as game-changing wonder drugs.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:09.009
But just how safe and effective
are they?

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.477
Why do most people
stop taking them

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.511
within a few months,

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.247
why does weight loss plateau,

00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:14.748
and what happens
when you quit?

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.984
I answer all these questions
and more

00:00:16.984 --> 00:00:22.389
in this video series on Ozempic
and other GLP-1 drugs.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:28.829
"Are GLP-1 Drugs Like Ozempic (Semaglutide)
Game Changers for Weight Loss?"

00:00:28.829 --> 00:00:31.131
The new class
of weight-loss drugs,

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:34.234
GLP-1 agonists like Ozempic,

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:38.071
have received enormous,
almost unprecedented, attention

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.706
in the mainstream media.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:43.977
They’ve been called "the medical
sensation of the decade."

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:47.047
The business press
was practically giddy,

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:50.851
declaring the end
of the obesity epidemic.

00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:53.754
The enthusiasm is shared
in the medical literature,

00:00:53.754 --> 00:00:54.788
with headlines suggesting

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:57.524
they are game-changing
revolutions

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.026
in the treatment of obesity:

00:00:59.026 --> 00:01:01.728
therapeutic-wizard miracle drugs

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:05.465
that are hugely effective
in the treatment of obesity.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:10.437
But history is littered with
failed weight-loss wonder drugs.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.272
Every other year or so,

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:15.008
an anti-obesity medication
that had been approved

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.276
to be safe and effective

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:18.478
has had to be withdrawn
from the market

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:21.782
after serious side effects
emerged.

00:01:21.782 --> 00:01:25.118
See my video on the subject
for the whole sordid story

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:28.155
of how these so-called
medical magic bullets

00:01:28.155 --> 00:01:31.825
have turned out to be blanks,
or worse.

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:35.195
To date, most weight-loss drugs,
despite their initial approval,

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.497
have since been
pulled from the market

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.232
for unforeseen side effects

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.802
that have turned them
into a public threat.

00:01:41.802 --> 00:01:45.205
From "rainbow diet pills"
packed with amphetamines

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.573
that were marketed to women,

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.875
to the rise and fall of fen-phen

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.545
(which triggered catastrophic
heart and lung conditions),

00:01:51.545 --> 00:01:54.081
history is beset
by failures to find

00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:57.050
safe, successful
weight-loss drugs.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.354
Aminorex was a widely prescribed
appetite suppressant

00:02:00.354 --> 00:02:02.956
before it was pulled
for causing lung damage.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.759
Eighteen million Americans
were on fen-phen

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:08.662
before it was pulled for causing
severe damage to heart valves.

00:02:08.662 --> 00:02:11.932
Meridia was pulled
for heart attacks and strokes,

00:02:11.932 --> 00:02:15.535
and Acomplia for psychiatric
side effects, including suicide.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.971
Belviq was withdrawn in 2020

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.574
after it was recognized that
it may have been causing cancer

00:02:20.574 --> 00:02:22.976
for the eight years
it had been on the market.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.611
The U.S. Food and Drug
Administration

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:27.381
initially rejected it
after it appeared to cause

00:02:27.381 --> 00:02:30.017
several types of tumors in rats,

00:02:30.017 --> 00:02:33.787
but when a one-year human trial
showed no apparent cancer,

00:02:33.787 --> 00:02:36.123
it was approved
and went on to become

00:02:36.123 --> 00:02:38.825
one of the most frequently
prescribed weight-loss drugs.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:42.429
But when people were actually
on it for a few years,

00:02:42.429 --> 00:02:45.332
notably high rates of colorectal
cancer, pancreatic cancer,

00:02:45.332 --> 00:02:46.533
and lung cancer popped up;

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:50.537
so, oopsey,
it was pulled from the market.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:52.873
The news was met
with surprise and confusion

00:02:52.873 --> 00:02:54.841
among obesity medicine
specialists,

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.543
who had been
prescribing the drug

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:58.145
to help patients
achieve and sustain

00:02:58.145 --> 00:03:00.147
the health benefits
of weight loss.

00:03:00.147 --> 00:03:02.215
It was particularly jarring,

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:06.286
because the drug was generally
regarded as being so safe,

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.422
until it wasn’t.

00:03:08.422 --> 00:03:11.191
Or take Benfluorex,
like Ozempic,

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:14.694
another diabetes drug repurposed
as an appetite suppressant.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.030
It caused hundreds of deaths,

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.600
but didn’t get pulled
for 33 years.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.571
The drug company knew about
the risks, but covered them up.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:27.207
Judges concluded
that the drug company’s priority

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.409
was systematically given to

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:32.079
"preserving
its own economic interests

00:03:32.079 --> 00:03:35.682
over the safety
of the drug’s consumers."

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.151
So, historically,
anti-obesity drugs have been

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.786
kind of like cigarettes.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.254
Like smoking,

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.457
popping these pills
can cause you to lose weight,

00:03:43.457 --> 00:03:45.425
but at what cost?

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:49.563
The goal of weight loss is not
to fit into a skinnier casket.

00:03:49.563 --> 00:03:52.199
But they don’t even work
very well.

00:03:52.199 --> 00:03:56.403
The current crop of
approved meds includes Qsymia,

00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:59.172
a combination of phentermine,
the phen in fen-phen,

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:01.842
and topiramate, a drug
that can cause seizures

00:04:01.842 --> 00:04:04.111
if you abruptly stop taking it.

00:04:04.111 --> 00:04:06.880
This drug combination
was explicitly rejected

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:09.349
multiple times
for safety reasons in Europe

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:12.452
but remains for sale
in the United States.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.820
Contrave is another option,

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.256
if you choose to ignore
its own black-box warning

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.825
about a potential increase
in suicidal thoughts.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:22.529
Alli, also sold as Xenical,
is the final choice.

00:04:22.529 --> 00:04:25.098
That’s the drug
that blocks fat absorption

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:29.669
and causes side effects such
as "flatus with discharge."

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:32.506
The drug evidently "forces
the patient to use diapers

00:04:32.506 --> 00:04:33.640
and to know the location

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.175
of all the bathrooms
in the neighborhood

00:04:35.175 --> 00:04:37.477
in an attempt
to limit the consequences

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:41.681
of urgent leakage
of oily fecal matter."

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:45.218
All for a grand total
of just 3 percent weight loss.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:48.321
All that mess to go from, like,
300 pounds (135 kg)

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.757
down to 291 pounds (130 kg).

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.993
As you can see,
older weight-loss medications

00:04:52.993 --> 00:04:55.795
only achieved about
5 percent weight loss,

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:59.699
whereas the newfangled
GLP-1 agonists like Ozempic

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.101
can cause an average of...

00:05:01.101 --> 00:05:03.570
6 percent weight loss!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.906
Now, this is because they were
averaging the effects

00:05:05.906 --> 00:05:10.710
of some of the older GLP-1
agonists like Saxenda or Byetta.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.480
Semaglutide,
sold as Ozempic for diabetes

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.682
and Wegovy for weight loss,

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:17.651
causes about twice that.

00:05:17.651 --> 00:05:21.988
And now, there’s tirzepatide,
sold as Mounjaro or Zepbound,

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:27.127
which gets you closer to what
you see with bariatric surgery.

00:05:27.127 --> 00:05:29.462
So, while the older
obesity medications achieve

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:32.199
weight losses in
the 5 to 10 percent range,

00:05:32.199 --> 00:05:33.967
the new generation of agents

00:05:33.967 --> 00:05:36.303
are more in
the 15 to 20 percent range,

00:05:36.303 --> 00:05:39.839
about triple what we saw
in many of the older drugs.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.107
So, for about half a century,

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.742
there’s been healthy skepticism

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:45.612
about new-kid-on-the-block
obesity drugs

00:05:45.612 --> 00:05:47.113
promising profound weight loss,

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:50.617
only to see one after another
fail and flop,

00:05:50.617 --> 00:05:55.222
but today, this historical
narrative could be in flux.

00:05:55.222 --> 00:05:59.526
How well do these new GLP-1
agonist drugs really work?

00:05:59.526 --> 00:06:00.560
How do they work?

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.262
How long do they work?

00:06:02.262 --> 00:06:03.964
What are
the short-term side effects?

00:06:03.964 --> 00:06:06.032
What are
the long-term side effects?

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:09.035
Are there cheaper, safer,
natural alternatives

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.371
to boost GLP-1
with diet and lifestyle?

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.807
What even is GLP-1?

00:06:13.807 --> 00:06:18.578
I’ll cover all those topics
and more next.

